#!/bin/bash
# All mock cases (fixtures regenerated by gen.py), 8 at a time; one line each; then TOTAL. Exit 0 only when every case
# gives its expected result and every script passes bash -n / sh -n (and shellcheck -S error when installed). No lamp.
M=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd); KIT=$(cd $M/.. && pwd); bad=0
for f in $KIT/run.sh $KIT/gate/*.sh $M/*.sh; do case $f in *.lamp.sh) continue;; esac; bash -n $f || { echo "SYNTAX $f"; bad=1; }; done
for f in $KIT/gate/*.lamp.sh; do cat $KIT/gate/common.lamp.sh $f | sh -n || { echo "SYNTAX $f"; bad=1; }; done
python3 -I -m py_compile $KIT/gate/eval.py $M/gen.py $M/bin/ssh || bad=1
if command -v shellcheck >/dev/null; then shellcheck -S error -s bash $KIT/run.sh $KIT/gate/kit.sh $KIT/gate/core.sh $KIT/gate/summary.sh || bad=1; fi
[ $bad = 0 ] && echo "SYNTAX OK (bash -n, sh -n, py_compile)"
# the kit never sets a volume: no amixer set, no osascript set volume, no write to the speaker's files
grep -rnE 'amixer [^|]*(set|sset)|set volume|> *\$KVOL|> *\$BVOL|speaker/volume.*(set|>)' $KIT/run.sh $KIT/gate | grep -vE ':[0-9]+: *#' | grep . && { echo "VOLUME WRITE found"; bad=1; } || echo "NO VOLUME WRITE (grep)"
grep -rnE 'systemctl (stop|restart|disable|mask) lamp-cloud|factory|forget.?all' $KIT/run.sh $KIT/gate | grep -vE ':[0-9]+: *#' | grep . && { echo "CLOUD/RESET found"; bad=1; } || echo "NO CLOUD STOP, RESET OR FORGET-ALL (grep)"
python3 -I $M/gen.py $M/fx || exit 1; rm -rf $M/work
ls $M/fx | xargs -P ${J:-8} -n1 $M/run-case.sh | sort | tee $M/results.txt
ok=$(grep -c ' OK ' $M/results.txt); mm=$(grep -c ' MISMATCH ' $M/results.txt); n=$(ls $M/fx | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
echo "TOTAL $n cases: OK $ok MISMATCH $mm"; [ "$ok" = "$n" ] && [ $bad = 0 ]
